Add an opt-in intra refresh capability

Carried from upstream https://github.com/moonlight-stream/moonlight-common-c/pull/97
(open as of 2026-08-12). Drop this patch and bump the submodule once it merges.

Sunshine has had the server half of this since LizardByte/Sunshine#3415 merged on
2024-12-23; only the client half is missing. rtsp.cpp try_emplace()s
"x-ss-video[0].intraRefresh" with a default of "0" and video.h carries it through to
nvenc_base.cpp as enableIntraRefresh, so the encoder emits a rolling intra refresh wave
instead of periodic IDR frames. That trades the bitrate spike and the visible hitch of a
full IDR for recovery spread over many frames, which matters most on the loss-prone paths
this fork already cares about.

Opt-in by design, and off unless the renderer sets CAPABILITY_INTRA_REFRESH: the Xbox
client reports visible corruption on static and low-complexity content, and Sunshine
honours the flag only on NVENC, so it is inert on AMD and Intel hosts. The client-side
setting that drives the bit is default-off for the same reason.

0x80 is free - Limelight.h uses 0x1 through 0x40 for the existing renderer capabilities
and CAPABILITY_SLICES_PER_FRAME() lives in bits 24 and up. The attribute is added inside
the existing IS_SUNSHINE() block in getAttributesList(), so GameStream hosts never see it,
and emitting "0" when opted out matches the default Sunshine already assumes.

diff --git a/src/Limelight.h b/src/Limelight.h
index b2bb5509..e1758b23 100644
--- a/src/Limelight.h
+++ b/src/Limelight.h
@@ -272,6 +272,10 @@ typedef struct _DECODE_UNIT {
 // supports reference frame invalidation for AV1 streams. This flag is only valid on video renderers.
 #define CAPABILITY_REFERENCE_FRAME_INVALIDATION_AV1 0x40

+// If set in the video renderer capabilities field, this flag specifies that the renderer
+// needs to opt-in to intra refresh, some clients (like the Xbox client with NVEnc) needs it
+#define CAPABILITY_INTRA_REFRESH 0x80
+
 // If set in the video renderer capabilities field, this macro specifies that the renderer
 // supports slicing to increase decoding performance. The parameter specifies the desired
 // number of slices per frame. This capability is only valid on video renderers.
diff --git a/src/SdpGenerator.c b/src/SdpGenerator.c
index a2f9789f..1aedad31 100644
--- a/src/SdpGenerator.c
+++ b/src/SdpGenerator.c
@@ -309,6 +309,13 @@ static PSDP_OPTION getAttributesList(char*urlSafeAddr) {
         else {
             err |= addAttributeString(&optionHead, "x-ss-video[0].chromaSamplingType", "0");
         }
+
+        // Add intra-refresh if opted in
+        if (VideoCallbacks.capabilities & CAPABILITY_INTRA_REFRESH){
+            err |= addAttributeString(&optionHead, "x-ss-video[0].intraRefresh", "1");
+        } else {
+            err |= addAttributeString(&optionHead, "x-ss-video[0].intraRefresh", "0");
+        }
     }

     snprintf(payloadStr, sizeof(payloadStr), "%d", StreamConfig.width);
